In `uniq`, the brute-force fallback starts by assigning `seen = []` and then executing `for e in c:`. A loop-header observation for that outer loop happens before the body of the first iteration, so `seen` is still empty then, making `len(seen) > 0` false. The test suite includes non-empty containers that reach this fallback, so that first loop-header state is observed; it also includes an empty container, where the loop header is checked with `seen` still empty. Therefore the condition does not hold at every observed outer-loop-header event.

